  "body": "The `wire_stamp` test binary on upstream main did not compile because its complete `WireContourOp` fixture omitted the `taper_deg` field introduced by wire constant taper support. Add `taper_deg: 0.0` explicitly to all five `WireContourOp` literals in `crates/app/tests/wire_stamp.rs`, including the four struct-update expressions, as requested. These tests continue to model straight wire cuts.\n\nThe branch starts at the latest fetched upstream main, `ee05ba87`. Only the test file changes; no product code, dependencies, snapshots, or golden files change. The fork remains synced at v0.18.0; this issue branch uses upstream main directly as explicitly requested.\n\nValidation on Linux x86-64:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_stamp` — passed all 3 tests: `an_open_runs_side_and_clearance_each_mark_its_path_stale`, `the_four_sides_stamp_apart_and_a_closed_cut_ignores_the_clearance`, and `an_unrelated_edit_and_a_round_trip_leave_the_cuts_ok`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` — passed.\n- `git diff --check` — passed. The diff is limited to the five zero-taper initializations in the requested test file.\n\nThe requested checks were run on the final five-literal diff. Other platforms and the full workspace test suite were not run for this test-only initializer fix.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only).\nEffort: low; no escalation.\n\nFixes #1377\n",
